<https://github.com/DynamicalSystemsGroup/sysml-concept-reference/id/profile/part-usage>
    dct:description "Describes a system or system part in a context. A definition describes its kind; multiple usages can share that kind." ;
    rdf:type inv:ConceptProfile ;
    inv:caveat "No exhaustive permission matrix or complete notation grammar is claimed.", "The examples have been checked against source notation, but no SysML parser or semantic engine was run." ;
    inv:concept <https://github.com/DynamicalSystemsGroup/sysml-concept-reference/id/SysML/20250201/Systems-Parts-PartUsage> ;
    inv:evidence <https://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/2.0/Language/PDF#page=321>, <https://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/2.0/Language/PDF#page=90> ;
    inv:evidenceStatus inv:EditorialSummary ;
    inv:hasExample <https://github.com/DynamicalSystemsGroup/sysml-concept-reference/id/example/part-usage> ;
    inv:hasNotation <https://github.com/DynamicalSystemsGroup/sysml-concept-reference/id/notation/part-node> ;
    inv:hasRelationship <https://github.com/DynamicalSystemsGroup/sysml-concept-reference/id/profile/part-usage/relationship/1>, <https://github.com/DynamicalSystemsGroup/sysml-concept-reference/id/profile/part-usage/relationship/2>, <https://github.com/DynamicalSystemsGroup/sysml-concept-reference/id/profile/part-usage/relationship/3> ;
    inv:learningPoint "A referential part remains a PartUsage. It is not converted into the metaclass ReferenceUsage just because its declaration contains ref.", "Owning a part declaration, featuring its values, and making those values composite are separate mechanisms.", "The declared partDefinition property has multiplicity 0..*. Class-level constraints still require at least one applicable PartDefinition typing; declaration cardinality alone is not the whole rule.", "The normalized defaults below describe metamodel fields. The multiplicity and composition of a part in a user model follow contextual SysML rules." ;
    inv:profilePage "concepts/part-usage.md" ;
    inv:profileStatus inv:DraftSourceChecked .

